WEBVTT

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:32.250
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The sergeant at arms is directed to make a proclamation.

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:44.490
Alfredo Sotto Corpuz: All persons are commanded to keep silent under pain of penalty while the impeachment court is in session for the trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:50.530
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte is hereby called to order.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:57.650
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: We shall be led in prayer by Senator-Judge Christopher Bong Go.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:06.850
Sen. Christopher Bong Go: Let us put ourselves in the presence of the Lord.

00:08:09.170 --> 00:11:11.510
Sen. Christopher Bong Go: Almighty God, we come before you today seeking your wisdom, guidance, and strength as we fulfill the duties entrusted to us by the Filipino people. We pray for the peaceful conduct of the ongoing BARM elections and and for the continued success of the Bangsamoro Peace Process. Matagal nang pinagdadaanan ng ating mga kapatid sa Bangsamoro ang landas tungo sa kapayapaan. Naway magiging pagkakataon ng halalan upang mas marinig ang boses ng taong bayan at lalo pang mapagtibay ang kapayapaan, pagkakaisa, at pagunlad sa rehyon. Kami rin po ay pinili ng taong bayan upang maging kanilang mga kinatawan. Nawa'y huwag naming sayangin ang tiwalang ipinagkaloob nila sa amin sapagkat sa aming mga disisyon ay nakasalalay hindi lamang ang kasalukuyan kundi maging ang kinabukasan ng ating bansa at ng mga susunod na henerasyon. In this important moment for our nation, grant us clarity of mind and sincerity of heart. May we always be guided by truth, fairness, respect for our institutions, and above all, the welfare of every Filipino. Lord, as we perform our solemn duty as Senator-Judges, remind us that the credibility and integrity of this Court rests upon how faithfully and fairly we discharge our responsibilities. Tayo ang pinili at pinagkatiwalaan ng mahalagang tungkulin ito, naway maging patas at makatarungan kami sa bawat hakbang at disisyon aming gagawin. Lord, We also pray for our countrymen who continue to face the daily struggles of life sa gitna ng hirap ng buhay, pagtaas ng mga bilihin, mga sakuna, at iba pang pagsubok. Tulungan mo kaming huwag malimutan ang tunay na dahilan ng aming paglilingkod, ang mapabuti ang buhay ng bawat Pilipino. May this process never divide us as a nation, sa halip naway manaig ang ating pagkakabuklod-buklod Pagalang sa isa't isa at pagmamalasakit sa kapwa. I am for unity. I am for healing of this country. Sana matapos na ito para makatrabaho na tayo. Remind us that beyond our positions and responsibilities, we share one country and one responsibility to protect its people in its future. Guide each one of us to act according to our conscience, the Constitution, and the rule of law. Give us the humility to listen, the courage to do what is right, and the wisdom to place the interests of the Filipino people above all else. May our decisions contribute to a stronger, more peaceful, more united, and healed Philippines. All these we ask in your holy name. Amen.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:12:04.160
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Senator-Judge Pia S. Cayetano, Senator-Judge Ronald "Bato" M. dela Rosa, Senator-Judge Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito, Senator-Judge Jinggoy Ejercito Estrada, Senator-Judge Christopher Bong Go, Senator-Judge Risa Hontiveros, Senator-Judge Panfilo "Ping" M. Lacson, Senator-Judge Manuel "Lito" M. Lapid, Senator-Judge Loren Legarda, Senator-Judge Rodante Marcoleta, Senator-Judge Imee Marcos, Senator-Judge Robinhood "Robin" Padilla, Senator-Judge Francis "Kiko" Pangilinan, Senator-Judge Vicente "Tito" C. Sotto III, Senator-Judge Erwin Tulfo, Senator-Judge Raffy T. Tulfo, Senator-Judge Joel Villanueva, Senator-Judge Camille Villar, Senator-Judge Mark A. Villar, Senator-Judge Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri, the Presiding Officer, Senator-Judge Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero, Senate President, Senator-Judge Sherwin T. Gatchalian.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:08.860
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: With 17 Senator-judges present, the Chair declares the presence of a quorum.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:20.460
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: In accordance with the rules of procedure on impeachment trials, the Chair now recognizes the duly elected Presiding Officer to preside over the proceedings of the Impeachment Court.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:36.320
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Mr. Senate President. If there are no objections, we shall dispense with the reading of the September 14, 2026 Journal of the Senate sitting as an impeachment court and consider the same as approved. The Clerk of Court will please call the case before the impeachment court.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:42.720
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Case number 004-2026 in the matter of impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:44.480
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Appearances of the parties.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:50.980
Rep. Terry L. Ridon: For the prosecution, magandang umaga po. We are ready, Your Honors. Good morning,

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:52.700
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Honorable Ridon. For the respondent?

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:55.020
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Good morning, Your Honor. Same appearance for the defense.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:13:01.060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Good morning, Atty. Sheila. Who is your witness for this morning, Honorable Ridon?

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:06.600
Rep. Terry L. Ridon: Handa po kami i-presenta si Atty. Karen Batu ng Office of the Ombudsman.

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:08.680
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Who will be presenting the witness?

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:15.700
Rep. Terry L. Ridon: It will be Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih, member of the panel of the prosecutors.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.340
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel for the panel of prosecutors.

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:45.210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Atty. James, call your witness.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:14:07.110
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Good morning, Your Honor. It's a pleasure to be in your presence today. For the record, again, I am James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih of PECABAR Law, appearing as counsel for the prosecutors. With your kind permission, Your Honor, we would like to call to the witness stand Atty. Karen S. Batu, the officer in charge of the Central Records Division of the Office of the Ombudsman.

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:12.950
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly situate Atty. Karen Batu to the witness stand.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:21.450
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The clerk of court is directed to administer the oath to Attorney Batu.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:41.130
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Ma'am, please raise your right hand. You, Karen S. Batu, do swear that the evidence you shall give in the case now pending between the Philippines and Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte shall be the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth. So help you God.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:47.100
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Maganda umaga po, Attorney Batu. Naunawaan niyo po ang pinanumpaan ninyo?

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:48.540
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, Your Honor.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:51.240
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Okay, your witness, Attorney James,

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:52.120
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: kindly

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:53.140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: make your offer.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:15:59.190
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Yes, your honor. Good morning again, your honors, and also good morning to our friends from the defense. Chief, good morning. Good morning, James. All right. Your honor, we are presenting Attorney Batu for the following purposes. Number one, and for ease of reference, your honor, the same are being flashed on screen. So number one, to prove that The witness is the officer in charge of the records division of the Office of the Ombudsman and has been serving in such capacity since December 2025. Number two, to prove that the Office of the Ombudsman is the official repository of the statements of assets, liabilities, and net worth. And for brevity or honor, allow me to refer to this as SAL-N throughout these proceedings of constitutional, national, and local elective officials, including the SAL-Ns of the Vice President Sara Duterte for the years 2007 to 2012, and then from 2016 to 2020-25. Number three, to

00:16:01.660 --> 00:17:46.490
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: prove that the network declared by the Vice President in her SAL-Ns for 2007 to 2025 including its components like the amount of cash and other personal properties she declared for those years. Number four, to prove that based on the Vice President's own declarations under oath in her SALNs for 2007 to 2025, her declared net worth as well as that of her spouse, Atty. Manasseh Scarpio, increased from 7,250,497 pesos in 2007 65,308,841 in 2021 and later to 98,656,131.20 in 2025 or an increase of around 91 million from 2007. Number five, to prove that the Vice President did not declare any cash on hand, or cash in bank in her SAL-Ns for the years 2019 to 2025 after making cash declarations in her 2007 to 2012 and 2016 to 2018 SAL-Ns. Number 6. To prove that based on the official records of the Ombudsman, the Vice President's SAL-Ns contain no declaration of any foreign currency deposits, including deposits denominated in U.S. dollars or even other foreign currencies, all including Chinese RMB and the like.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:18:12.930
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Number seven, to prove that the Vice President Duterte declared under oath in her silence that she and or her spouse, Atty. Carpio, have various business and financial interests but failed to declare their ownership of the shares of stock and their corresponding acquisition, or cost or value rather. Number eight,

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:13.870
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: to

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:40.750
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: prove that despite her election as Vice President in June 2022 and as declared under oath in her SAL-N for the succeeding years, Vice President Duterte did not divest and instead willfully continued her business and financial interest. To emphasize, in Metro City Chow Foods Corporation, GenCorp Industries Inc., and other corporations.

00:18:42.380 --> 00:19:01.410
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Number nine, to identify your honors and authenticate the certified true copies of the SAL-Ns involving those years that I've mentioned. And lastly, to prove other material allegations in relation to the articles of impeachment. Thank you.

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:11.040
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Purpose number one, Your Honor, the defense is willing to stipulate,

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:11.420
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Your Honor.

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:33.020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: As well as number two, perhaps. However, there has to be a correction on number two, Your Honor, as I think they stated that the repository for all elective officials would be the Office of the Ombudsman. Just for accuracy's sake, Your Honor, regional and local elective officials, the repository is the Office of the Deputy Ombudsman in their respective region. We just want that clarified, Your Honor. What

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Do you say, Attorney James?

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:44.550
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Nevertheless, Your Honor, whether they are regional, Local. These are all still part of the Office of the Ombudsman so there's really no need for the nuancing. I think

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:58.050
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: the nuance is necessary in order to dispense with proving that Attorney Batu is aware of these salends filed when the Vice President was still Vice Mayor or Mayor.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:58.970
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Yes, Your Honor. Thank

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:00.150
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: you for understanding the point.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:09.150
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Yes, Your Honor. And in relation to that, I guess the next stipulation would also be, Your Honor, that all those SAL-Ns are true and authentic. Is that correct?

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:11.590
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: We are not willing to stipulate on that, Your Honor.

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:15.200
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Proceed with your comments, Attorney Justin.

00:20:15.200 --> 00:21:19.440
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Yes, Your Honor. We will proceed to our objections, Your Honor. Just to be clarified, we are particularly referring to purposes number 3, 4, and 9, Your Honor, as this refer to documents or SAL-Ns. Covering periods which the respondent was not an impeachable officer, Your Honor. This is the proper time to raise this because we are not objecting to the documentary evidence yet as it is not the proper time. But we are objecting to the offer of the testimonial evidence which the witness will be producing before this court today, Your Honor. Again, Your Honor, we reiterate the ruling of Duterte v. House of Representatives that only matters In relation to the impeachable term that are committed or done in the, allegedly, in the impeachable, in relation to the position, Your Honor, are matters that can be or within the ambit of this impeachment court, Your Honor. We are therefore objecting on the ground of irrelevance and inadmissibility, Your Honor, for the rest of the offer, Your Honor, subject to cross-examination.

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:20.930
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Your Honor, may we comment?

00:21:20.930 --> 00:22:49.320
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Your Honor? No need, so we can proceed. The chair would like to remind counsel for the respondent the ruling of the chair with respect to the issuance of the subpoenas covering the period 2007 up to 2025. That pursuant to OMB, Office of the Ombudsman v. Bernardo, GR 18-1598, dated March 2013, there is a necessity to establish the baseline. Not for the prosecution but equally for the respondent in order to find out what is the base figure for the computation of the salon during her term as vice president. The chair also clarified when it ruled in favor of granting the subpoena that we are not adding to the charges against the vice president for supposed acts committed prior to her term as vice president. The only ones she's being charged of before the impeachment court would be those committed during her term as vice president from 2022 up to the present. And whatever it is that may be shown is only for purposes of establishing a baseline and not adding to the charges already made in the articles of impeachment that are outside her term. We will register your continuing objection, Attorney Justin. With respect to offers number 3, 4, and 9. Would that be correct?

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:50.140
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Yes, Your Honor.

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:51.500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Very well,

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:52.900
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Your Honor. Subject to cross. A

00:22:52.900 --> 00:23:02.940
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: continuing objection with respect to offers 3, 4, and 9 is hereby noted. Attorney James, your witness, you may proceed when you're ready. Salamat po and thank you

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:04.040
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: for the clarification, Your Honor.

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:16.330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: And again, Attorney James, to clarify, whatever the witness will say with respect to the period before the Vice President became Vice President is only for the establishment of a baseline.

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:18.610
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: That is precisely what we're about to do, Your Honor.

00:23:18.610 --> 00:23:19.310
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Please proceed,

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:19.610
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel.

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:21.690
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Good

00:23:21.690 --> 00:23:22.310
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: morning, Madam Witness.

00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:22.950
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Good morning.

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:28.970
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Would you mind telling us first your personal circumstances for the record, please?

00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:37.100
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I'm attorney Karen S. Batu. I'm the officer in charge of the Central Records Division of the Office of the Ombudsman. Madam

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:44.420
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Witness, at any time if you cannot understand my question, please feel free to correct me or to ask for a clarification. Is that okay?

00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:44.980
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, sir.

00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:49.850
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Thank you, po. Sige. I understand that you're also a lawyer. Is that right?

00:23:50.290 --> 00:23:50.930
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, sir.

00:23:51.130 --> 00:23:53.090
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: How long have you been a member of the bar, please?

00:23:53.970 --> 00:23:59.530
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I took the bar in 2014 and passed the bar. I became a member of the bar in 2015.

00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:04.410
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: And how long have you been working in the office of the ombudsman?

00:24:04.850 --> 00:24:07.510
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I've been with the office of the ombudsman since 2010.

00:24:08.390 --> 00:24:08.830
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: 2010.

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:15.960
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: From 2010, what other positions, if any, have you held in the office of the ombudsman?

00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:36.600
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I started as a graph prevention and control officer with the Public Assistance and Corruption Prevention Office. And then, after passing the bar, I got promoted to the position of graph investigation officer 1. And I was assigned at the ombudsman proper. Prior to that, the overall deputy ombudsman office.

00:24:38.970 --> 00:24:46.070
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Just last year, I got promoted to the position of Graft Investigation and Prosecution Officer III.

00:24:46.370 --> 00:24:50.650
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Sige po. Ma'am, just to clarify, pwede po kayo mag-Tagalog or English kung

00:24:50.650 --> 00:24:51.150
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: saan po kayo

00:24:51.150 --> 00:24:51.930
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: komportable po?

00:24:52.030 --> 00:24:52.550
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tama po.

00:24:52.550 --> 00:24:52.910
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Sige po.

00:24:53.710 --> 00:25:02.750
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Okay. Sige po. Nabanggit niyo po na kayo ay nasa OIC ng CRD or Central Records Division. Tama po? Tama

00:25:02.750 --> 00:25:02.930
Atty. Karen S. Batu: po.

00:25:03.110 --> 00:25:05.130
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Ano naman po itong CRD po na ito?

00:25:05.710 --> 00:25:24.570
Atty. Karen S. Batu: The Central Records Division is a frontline service of the Office of the Ombudsman in charge of the case records management which include receiving, releasing, the storing, and eventual disposing of these documents such as complaints.

00:25:28.150 --> 00:25:30.130
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Pleadings, Salens, and Letters.

00:25:30.950 --> 00:25:33.290
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Complaints, Pleadings, Salens, and Letters.

00:25:33.450 --> 00:25:33.910
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: But

00:25:33.910 --> 00:25:42.750
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: for purposes of today's hearing, let's just focus on Salen. At paulit-ulit na po natin narinig ito. From the Ombudsman, ano po ba ang Salen?

00:25:43.570 --> 00:25:56.290
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Ang SALN po, based po sa RA 6713, ito po ay isang statement made under oath. It's a declaration under oath of a public official.

00:25:57.950 --> 00:26:05.310
Atty. Karen S. Batu: pertaining to his or her assets, liabilities, net worth, including the spouses.

00:26:05.970 --> 00:26:15.930
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Okay. Pagpasensya niyo na mama, hindi pa kasi ako nagdo-government so I'm not familiar with SAL-N. But when you say that SAL-Ns are under oath, ano po bang ibig sabihin nun?

00:26:16.450 --> 00:26:18.410
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Ito po ay sinumpaang salaysay.

00:26:18.530 --> 00:26:18.910
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Nino?

00:26:19.170 --> 00:26:21.290
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Nang declarant or nang public official.

00:26:21.770 --> 00:26:29.360
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: So ibig sabihin po, and this is just confirmatory, Yung SAL-N, pinapanumpaan nung deklarant, ano yung pinapanumpaan niya?

00:26:29.740 --> 00:26:34.040
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Na ito yung natutoo yung mga nilagay niya dun sa SAL-N. Natutoo

00:26:34.040 --> 00:26:35.640
Atty. Karen S. Batu: yung nasa laman ng SAL

00:26:35.640 --> 00:26:35.860
Atty. Karen S. Batu: -N.

00:26:36.550 --> 00:26:38.330
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: At nagpo-file din kayo ng SAL-N, tama?

00:26:38.990 --> 00:26:39.650
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, sir.

00:26:39.810 --> 00:26:41.650
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: At nanunumpa kayo na tama yung SAL-N niyo?

00:26:41.810 --> 00:26:42.310
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, sir.

00:26:42.550 --> 00:26:47.790
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Very good. Sige po. At sino naman po yung required na mag-file ng SAL-Ns?

00:26:48.810 --> 00:26:52.450
Atty. Karen S. Batu: All officials of the government except for

00:26:53.960 --> 00:27:02.280
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I think those who are in honorary capacity, mga laborers and those

00:27:04.680 --> 00:27:07.240
Atty. Karen S. Batu: on contractual, mga casual employees.

00:27:07.560 --> 00:27:11.780
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Okay, wait. So yung nabanggit niyong tatlo, sila yung hindi kailangan mag-file?

00:27:11.780 --> 00:27:12.220
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Hindi po,

00:27:12.220 --> 00:27:12.480
Atty. Karen S. Batu: hindi.

00:27:12.480 --> 00:27:16.520
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: But all other public officials must file a SAL-ED, is that correct?

00:27:16.760 --> 00:27:17.000
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes.

00:27:17.300 --> 00:27:20.100
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: And perhaps that includes the Vice President?

00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:20.820
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes.

00:27:21.120 --> 00:27:26.340
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: And in relation to what you mentioned a while ago, Regardless, whether it's a

00:27:26.340 --> 00:27:33.120
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: public official or the vice president herself, pinapanumpaan nila na tama yung laman ng SAL-N na yun.

00:27:33.140 --> 00:27:34.880
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Asked and answered and leading, Your Honor.

00:27:34.920 --> 00:27:36.560
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: We'll just proceed, Your Honor, to the next point.

00:27:36.560 --> 00:27:38.220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Move to the next point, Attorney James.

00:27:38.220 --> 00:27:40.100
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Thank you, po. Sige.

00:27:42.220 --> 00:27:49.620
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Madam Witness, do you recall receiving a letter dated June 16 from the House of Representatives?

00:27:51.050 --> 00:27:52.880
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes. And

00:27:52.880 --> 00:28:02.000
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: in that letter, there was a request for you to submit the sal-ends of the Vice President from 2007 to 2025. Is that correct?

00:28:02.300 --> 00:28:02.840
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, sir.

00:28:03.040 --> 00:28:06.600
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: And what actions, if any, have you taken in relation to that letter?

00:28:07.200 --> 00:28:10.840
Atty. Karen S. Batu: We prepared the sal-ends and then submitted it to the House of Representatives.

00:28:12.020 --> 00:28:15.720
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: And if the sal-ends are shown to you, would you be able to identify this?

00:28:16.060 --> 00:28:16.340
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes.

00:28:16.720 --> 00:28:34.040
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Your Honor, at this point, may I respectfully ask that Atty. Luis Perez, my assisting lawyer, also from Pekabar Lawyer Honor, to assist me in confronting the witness with the documents and perhaps to check the witness from time to time if she's still okay.

00:28:34.440 --> 00:28:46.260
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Attorney Luis is authorized. Also, corresponding assisting counsel from the respondent is also equally authorized to approach the witness at any point in time while she is testifying.

00:28:46.480 --> 00:28:47.680
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Salamat po. Please

00:28:47.680 --> 00:28:48.140
