Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Tama nga po yung sagot niyo. Walang nakalagay na acquisition cost pero hindi rin po kasi hinihiling sa SAL-N na ilagay yung acquisition cost ng business interest. Tama po ba? Dahil kung gusto niyo pong ilagay, saan niyo po lalagay?

01:36:08.300 --> 01:36:20.920
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Ang tanong, if I may clarify your honor, ang pagkakaintindi ko po sa tanong sa akin kanina ni Atty. James is

01:36:22.690 --> 01:36:28.550
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Unang tanong po niya kasi is kung merong nakadeclare sa personal properties na stocks.

01:36:28.930 --> 01:36:47.850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi po. Yung unang bahagi ng tanong ay kaugnay sa acquisition cost ng business interest ng stock ng shareholdings. So, wala pong nakalagay. Tama po yun. Hindi po kayo nagsabi ng hindi totoo. Pero para klaruhin lang po natin, wala rin naman pong puwang, blanco, table, parte.

01:36:55.150 --> 01:37:03.930
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Sa mga business interests and financial connections, your honor, wala pong nakalagay na para sa acquisition costs.

01:37:13.420 --> 01:37:19.500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Sa inyong tanggapan sa Luzon, Visayas at Mindanao, sa local officials, gayon din sa President at Vice President. Tama po ba?

01:37:19.720 --> 01:37:21.880
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tama po, Your Honor.

01:37:21.880 --> 01:37:23.340
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ano po yung inyong

01:37:23.340 --> 01:37:34.100
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: review and compliance procedure kung meron man bilang repository ng salen ng Pangulo, ikalawang Pangulo at mga head ng executive agencies?

01:37:36.600 --> 01:37:48.740
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Ang Review and Compliance Committee po usually is sa mga head of the agencies po. Tapos sinasubmit na lang po nila sa Office of the Ombudsman as the repository agency.

01:37:49.260 --> 01:37:50.220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi po kayo yan?

01:37:50.420 --> 01:37:51.280
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Hindi po kami yan.

01:37:51.580 --> 01:37:55.420
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Sa loob po ng Office of the Ombudsman meron po kayong Compliance and Review Committee?

01:37:55.780 --> 01:37:58.700
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Para po sa mga empleyado ng Ombudsman, Your Honor, meron po.

01:37:59.080 --> 01:38:01.140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ano po yung alam niyong procedure kaugnay nun?

01:38:02.000 --> 01:38:05.460
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Nire-review po siya as to the form, usually, Your Honor. Kung

01:38:05.460 --> 01:38:06.600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: sumunod o hindi?

01:38:06.880 --> 01:38:07.100
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Apo.

01:38:07.640 --> 01:38:18.940
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, pag hindi po sumunod, papadalan presumably ng notification iyong empleyado na, Hoy, may hindi ka finilapan o Hoy, mali yung pagkaka-fill up mo. Gano 'n

01:38:18.940 --> 01:38:19.260
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: po ba yan?

01:38:19.560 --> 01:38:28.900
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Sa amin po, based on my experience, Your Honor, binalik po yung SAL-N at sinabi kung ano yung mga kailangang pil-upan or kung mali yung form na nagamit.

01:38:29.480 --> 01:38:38.580
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Lumipas na po ang April 30, binalik yung SAL-N. Ang sabihin na natin, Hunyo, pwede pong i-correct pa rin siya ng empleyado.

01:38:41.820 --> 01:38:49.640
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Pagdating po sa amin, Your Honor, April 30, ang submission po kasi based... Siyempre,

01:38:49.640 --> 01:39:02.450
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: doon po lang po nakita ng compliance interview committee niyo, di ba? Pag-submit. E din nakita niyo may kulang. Babalik niyo po. Sabi niyo nga po, di ba? Iko-correct niya. So sabihin natin, nabalik ng May 1, May 2.

01:39:04.470 --> 01:39:05.950
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Pwede po niya i-correct yun, di ba?

01:39:06.670 --> 01:39:18.680
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tama po, Your Honor. Kasi doon po sa SALN guidelines namin nakalagay na we still have until June 30 to submit the... SALNs to the repository agency.

01:39:19.430 --> 01:39:19.990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: To

01:39:19.990 --> 01:39:21.210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: the repository agency?

01:39:21.590 --> 01:39:21.970
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes po.

01:39:22.210 --> 01:39:31.330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Sa ibig sabihin po nun, pag na-submit na po kasi sa repository, hindi na po pwedeng baguhin. Di ba yun ang nakalagay sa Civil Service Memorandum Circular?

01:39:32.590 --> 01:39:33.730
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tama po, Your Honor.

01:39:34.010 --> 01:39:46.270
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Pero nakalagay din dun sa parehong GS Memorandum Circular ng Civil Service, pwedeng i-correct ng deklarant yung SALN niya. Sa susunod na taon, hindi po ba?

01:39:47.790 --> 01:39:49.710
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Ang requirement

01:39:49.710 --> 01:39:53.490
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: lang po is as long as it is based on honest mistake and or good faith.

01:39:54.230 --> 01:39:55.050
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, Your Honor.

01:39:57.490 --> 01:39:59.430
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Nagkamali ako ng deklarasyon ko ng 2025.

01:40:01.230 --> 01:40:09.060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: May nasulat ako mali doon. Sa susunod na taon, 2026, pag-file ko sa 2027, pwede ko i-correct yun.

01:40:09.830 --> 01:40:10.430
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Pwede

01:40:10.430 --> 01:40:10.750
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: po ba yan?

01:40:11.030 --> 01:40:19.510
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Again, Your Honor, I am not an expert as the Central Records Division is merely a repository of the records.

01:40:19.510 --> 01:40:19.830
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, but

01:40:19.830 --> 01:40:23.830
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: since you're a repository, you're aware the Vice President corrected herself and twice.

01:40:25.010 --> 01:40:28.690
Atty. Karen S. Batu: For 2025 po, meron po siyang sinadmit na amendment.

01:40:29.760 --> 01:40:35.660
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Actually, sa pagkakaalam ko, noong 2017 may sinadmit siyang amendment for 2016.

01:40:37.170 --> 01:40:45.410
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Sa 2016 sa ala niya at noong 2020 nag-submit siya ng pagbabago sa 2019 sa ala niya. That should be in your records, correct?

01:40:45.690 --> 01:40:56.050
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Ang nakalagay lang po na check po namin is for the 2025 po kasi after doong submission ng May medyo po ulit dumating noong June na amendment po.

01:40:56.490 --> 01:40:58.890
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So ang alam nyo lang po yung 2025 correction?

01:40:59.190 --> 01:41:07.230
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes. Ang ginagawa po kasi namin, Your Honor, basta yung mga SAL-Ns po, tinatanggap po namin yan basta sinubmit sa amin.

01:41:07.230 --> 01:41:18.790
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, you're saying based on your record, walang corrected SAL-N na sinubmit si Vice President Sara nung 2020 kaugnay sa 2019 SAL-N niya?

01:41:19.430 --> 01:41:26.170
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Based on our records, Your Honor, yun po yung mga SAL-Ns na sinubmit niya, yung mga binigay po namin sa House of Representatives.

01:41:26.670 --> 01:41:37.890
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, wala nga po kayong kopya nung dalawang SAL-N niya for 2019. Isang sinubmit ng June, isang sinubmit ng August 2020.

01:41:39.330 --> 01:41:48.000
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Based on our records po, yun lang po yung mga SAL-Ns na meron. Kung meron pong ibang SAL-N, wala po kaming nakita sa records namin.

01:41:48.120 --> 01:42:02.580
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Gayun din po sa SAL-N ng 2016, wala po kayong corrected SAL-N ng 2017 na sidabmit makalipas ang isang buwan ng April 30. Wala rin po. So tigitigisang SAL-N lang po sa lahat ng taon maliban sa 2025.

01:42:03.480 --> 01:42:12.100
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Meron pong ibuy your honor na parang kasi may exit SAL-N, so parang may dumoble. May exit SAL-N siya.

01:42:12.480 --> 01:42:13.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ano pong ibig sabihin ng exit

01:42:13.980 --> 01:42:20.160
Atty. Karen S. Batu: salen, ma'am? Parang nung matapos po yung term niya sa government for that year, nagsubmit siya ng salen niya.

01:42:20.560 --> 01:42:39.600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ginawa lang po yun noong June 30, ma'am, 2022. Dahil may bago po siyang posisyon, so kailangan niya magsubmit ng salen niya as of June 30, 2022. Matapos siyang mahalal bilang vicepresidente, nagsubmit po siya ng August 2022. Nagsubmit uli siya ng April...

01:42:41.260 --> 01:42:50.160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: 2023, kaugnay sa December 31, 2022, SAL-N niya. Yun po yung taon na dalawa talaga ang sinabit niya. Hindi po yun yung correction na sinasabi ko.

01:42:50.200 --> 01:42:55.160
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Opo. Pero based on our records, Your Honor, yun po yung dalawang, may dalawang SAL-N siya.

01:42:55.520 --> 01:42:57.540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yung ibang corrected po, wala na.

01:42:59.150 --> 01:43:14.020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yung ibang corrected na binabanggit ko po, wala na. Noong 2017, filing, kaugnay sa 2016, SAL-N, at yung 20... 20 filing kaugnay ng 2019 Sall-in na may sinubmit po siyang dalawang correction sa Sall-in niya.

01:43:15.220 --> 01:43:16.300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Wala po kayong copy nun?

01:43:16.300 --> 01:43:23.320
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Your Honor, based on our records, yun lang po yung mga Sall-ins na meron kami. Yun po yung sinubmit namin sa House of the Representatives.

01:43:23.320 --> 01:43:23.720
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Bilang

01:43:23.720 --> 01:43:28.900
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Mayor, sinasubmit po nila yan sa Deputy Ombudsman for Mindanao. Hindi po ba?

01:43:29.100 --> 01:43:29.900
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tama po, Your Honor.

01:43:29.900 --> 01:43:30.140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Lahat

01:43:30.140 --> 01:43:31.500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: po ba pino-forward sa inyo?

01:43:32.280 --> 01:43:34.940
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Hindi po. Sila din po yung repository nun, Your Honor.

01:43:35.620 --> 01:43:36.400
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi ikaw?

01:43:37.780 --> 01:43:47.200
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tell me po sa Central Records Division ang hawak lang po namin is the President, Vice President, the Constitutional Commissions po.

01:43:47.340 --> 01:43:53.080
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: But ma'am you testified on the SALN of the Vice President earlier before she became Vice President.

01:43:53.560 --> 01:44:03.480
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, Your Honor, because we requested upon receiving the subpoena of the House of Representatives, we requested those silence.

01:44:03.480 --> 01:44:03.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: But as a

01:44:03.980 --> 01:44:10.160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: natural course, hindi na po pinapadala sa inyo yung records pag hindi niyo po nire-request. Nandoon na

01:44:10.160 --> 01:44:10.680
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: po sa kanila.

01:44:10.720 --> 01:44:11.940
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, Your Honor. Okay.

01:44:12.500 --> 01:44:25.350
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator-Judge Pangilinan is recognized. We can entertain Senator-Judges until 12 noon to take advantage of the time. Senator-Judge Pangilinan, Senator-Judge Villanueva, thereafter, Senator-Judge Sotto.

01:44:26.130 --> 01:44:28.850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready.

01:44:28.850 --> 01:44:48.310
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. It's actually a follow-up to the points raised by the Presiding Officer. Atty. Batu, sabi po ninyo na noong 2017 at 20, yung walang corrected SALN in your possession, tama po ba?

01:44:48.370 --> 01:44:49.010
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Opo, Your Honor.

01:44:49.400 --> 01:45:09.020
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Dalawang beses daw kasi, according to our presiding officer, Kinorek. Would you know kung yung sinubmit ninyo sa House of Representatives and I would assume hanggang dito sa impeachment court, would you know if it was a corrected copy? Kasi sabi nyo isa lang eh. Or the original copy?

01:45:10.640 --> 01:45:12.360
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Your Honor, I... Kasi

01:45:12.360 --> 01:45:18.420
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: isa lang, di ba? Dalawang sinubmit, pero yung pangalawang dalawang sinubmit, corrected.

01:45:19.230 --> 01:45:19.710
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: So

01:45:19.710 --> 01:45:37.120
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: ang tanong ko, yung sinabit ba ninyo sa house as based on this subpoena ay yung corrected? Kaya isa lang? O yung hindi corrected? Would you know? Would you know? If

01:45:37.120 --> 01:45:37.360
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: you know.

01:45:37.360 --> 01:45:38.220
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Opo, Your Honor.

01:45:41.570 --> 01:46:02.030
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Prior to her tenure as the Vice President, sa Mindanao po kasi galing yun. Kasi sila po yung for the local government officials ng Mindanao area. So nung nag-request po kami sa kanila, upon receiving the subpoena from the House of the Representatives, yun po yung binigay nilang salihan sa amin, Your Honor.

01:46:02.650 --> 01:46:25.410
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, to answer Senator-Judge Pangilinan, actually what was submitted was not the corrected version because the correction only pertained to minor matters. The name of a relative that was omitted in 2019 and the address of her father, unofficial also at that time, in 2016.

01:46:26.990 --> 01:46:31.910
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So they did not reflect it anymore in the salin. It was simply contained in a letter. Correcting. Okay.

01:46:32.010 --> 01:46:35.750
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Thank you for the clarification, Mr. Presiding Officer. Maraming salamat, ma'am.

01:46:35.910 --> 01:46:36.450
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Thank you, po.

01:46:36.550 --> 01:46:42.080
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator-Judge Villanueva. Is recognized. You have two minutes, sir.

01:46:42.520 --> 01:46:43.080
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Yes,

01:46:43.080 --> 01:47:14.990
Sen. Joel Villanueva: thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer, Mr. President. Ma'am, just to be clear lang, under the rules applicable to each of the respondents' SALN in 2019 to 2024, para lang po malinaw yung timeline po. Kung mayroon po pang discrepancy sa SAL-N hanggang kailan po maaaring itama o kumpletuhin ang isang SAL-N matapos itong ma-file at anong particular event ang nagsasara po ng correction period?

01:47:16.000 --> 01:47:34.560
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Sir, from what I know, based on the omnibus SAL and guidelines, once it's submitted to the repository agency, parang you cannot have any amendments or changes. Final na po yun. That's the omnibus SAL and guidelines provisions po.

01:47:35.100 --> 01:48:00.050
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Patay po doon sa records na binabanggit po ninyo na kayo yung nagbabantay, ipinalam po ba? Sa respondent, Vice President, ang mga particular na discrepancy kung meron man na sinasabing nakita sa kanya pong salin at binibigyan po ba siya ng pagkakataong ipaliwanag o itama ang mga ito pag hindi pa napupunta dun sa repository?

01:48:00.910 --> 01:48:16.770
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I wouldn't know that sir kasi as I've said the office of the ombudsman is merely a repository agency so kung yung correction po dapat nasa review and compliance committee ng agency not with the office of the ombudsman po. So

01:48:16.770 --> 01:48:32.210
Sen. Joel Villanueva: pag na-receive po ang nangyayari lang po is that's it wala pong nagbe-verify or anything na ginagawa para kunyari po ma-ensure na yung na-submit na salin ay Kompleto po in form and in substance. Wala pong ganoon.

01:48:32.250 --> 01:48:51.890
Atty. Karen S. Batu: We just checked lang po kung halimbawa kasi ang nagsasubmit na po sa amin ng SAL-N is the head of the agency. So nagbibigay po yan ng list kung sino yung mga compliant, non-compliant, at hindi nagsasubmit pa. So biniverify lang po namin based on the listings kung nandun po yung mga pangalan ng mga SAL-Ns na yun.

01:48:52.140 --> 01:49:21.860
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Ibig sabihin pagdating po sa inyo, verified na yun ng form and substance. Salamat po. Isa na lang po dun sa maingat nating nais maintindihan tungkol po doon sa paglalamp ng cash on hand at cash in bank dun po sa item ng other personal assets. Ito po ba ay karaniwang ginagawa o unusual na yung cash in hand, cash in bank? Pwede mong ilamp doon sa other assets?

01:49:23.580 --> 01:49:38.680
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I'm not an expert pagdating sa mga ganyang usapin sa SAL-N and how other government officials filled out their SAL-Ns. So I cannot make any inference or conclusion as to that matter.

01:49:38.880 --> 01:50:26.660
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Tinanong ko po ito kasi doon sa 2025. 2025 lang po in-issue ng Civil Service yung guidelines na kung saan binabanggit po dito na dapat maging particular ka doon sa iyong tinatawag na cash declaration doon po sa section 26 ng memo guidelines nila. So ang tanong ko po, previously yung 2024, 2023, 2022, wala pa po itong guidelines na ito. Sa inyo pong pananaw bilang isang abogado at matagal na po nandyan sa ombudsman? Pupwede po ba na nung hindi pa lumalabas itong memo na ito ng 2025, pupwede po ba na ilump yung cash on hand o cash in bank doon po sa tinatawag na other assets po?

01:50:28.450 --> 01:50:34.830
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Your Honor, again, I'm not competent to answer that. I can only answer as to my own experience.

01:50:37.230 --> 01:50:45.780
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Parang even... Prior to this 2025 sale-in, nagde-declare na kami ng cash on hand, cash in bank separately.

01:50:46.320 --> 01:51:00.350
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Meaning sa inyong experience, even before the issuance of these guidelines, hindi nila lump sa other assets ang cash or cash in bank? In your experience.

01:51:00.670 --> 01:51:01.950
Atty. Karen S. Batu: In my experience, Your Honor.

01:51:01.950 --> 01:51:04.250
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Salamat po, Madam Vice. Thank you, Mr. President.

01:51:04.270 --> 01:51:12.790
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Without correcting the witness, the Chair would like to spread into the records Section 96 of the Omnibus Rules on Salen.

01:51:14.350 --> 01:51:58.790
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Corrective action after submission to repository agency. Upon submission of the original SAL-Ns with the Repository Agency, as outlined under Rule 9, corrections or amendments in the entries upon the initiative of the Declarant shall no longer be allowed. But it has a second paragraph. In the subsequent compliance on the filing of the SAL-N, any correction of entries non-disclosure of which was unintended or made in good faith shall be deemed a correction of the previous year's SALN. So, pwede po makorect sa susunod na taon kung based in good faith nga po. Senator-Judge Sotto is recognized. Apologies for the slight delay.

01:52:00.340 --> 01:52:16.850
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: No problem, Mr. Presiding Officer. Thank you very much. And just to support what Senator Villanueva has mentioned, for the record, and in addition to what you have mentioned, there is a Civil Service Commission resolution.

01:52:19.950 --> 01:52:44.330
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Number 1300174, issued January 24, 2013, which states that you have 30 days non-extendable from receipt of the order from your agency's head or office to complete or correct your SALN. Mayroong ganun pala silang Civil Service Commission. But I have only one question, Mr. President. And this is an issue na...

01:52:49.810 --> 01:52:50.490
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Atty.

01:52:56.520 --> 01:53:07.150
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Witness, a bank deposit denominated in a foreign currency is still an asset of the declarant, di po ba?

01:53:10.530 --> 01:53:12.890
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Hindi ko po masasagot yan, Your Honor.

01:53:20.170 --> 01:53:21.610
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Counsel for the Prosecution.

01:53:22.850 --> 01:53:23.250
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: What

01:53:23.250 --> 01:53:23.510
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: is the

01:53:23.510 --> 01:53:24.570
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: question, Your Honor? Again, sorry.

01:53:24.950 --> 01:53:33.330
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: A bank deposit denominated in foreign currency is still an asset of the declarant. Tama po ba?

01:53:33.450 --> 01:53:34.230
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Yes, of course, Your Honor.

01:53:34.430 --> 01:53:42.040
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Okay. Ganun din ano. The... Attorney Poa. Attorney Justin, go ahead.

01:53:42.040 --> 01:53:43.300
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Yes, Your Honor. Correct.

01:53:43.300 --> 01:53:43.620
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Okay.

01:53:43.900 --> 01:53:46.060
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Sorry, may I clarify the question, Your Honor?

01:53:46.300 --> 01:53:54.140
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Yung pong mga bank deposits na denominated in a foreign currency, dapat nakadeklara rin sa solid. Di po ba?

01:53:54.360 --> 01:54:01.400
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: We will defer the construction of the law to the impeachable, ah, to the Senator-Judges, Your Honor. We'd rather not comment on matters of law.

01:54:01.580 --> 01:54:10.780
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Ah, okay. Now, sa tagal niyo po doon, Attorney, sa Ombudsman, at saka repository kayo.

01:54:12.930 --> 01:54:25.750
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Nakikita niyo po ba na doon sa mga SALNs na ang mga nagde-deposit at nakasubmit ng mga SALNs sa inyo, doon sa cash on hand nila o cash on bank, may nagde-deklara ng foreign currency?

01:54:26.860 --> 01:54:46.900
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I'm sorry, Your Honor, but we do not check po isa-isa kung ano yung mga nakalagay po na mga items na dinideclare ng mga declarant natin. We merely check po as to the forms tapos po kung nasa list sila. Pero as to the details stated therein, hindi po namin yan chinecheck, Your Honor.

01:54:47.100 --> 01:55:10.320
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: So hindi mo, ikaw mismo, hindi mo napapansin na let's say doon sa cash on hand? Meron silang kung ilang milyon o ilang daan libo nakalagay, di ba? Ano, puro pesos ba nakikita niyo nun? Hindi, I'm not pertaining to the silence of the Vice President. Doon sa mga dati ninyo, sa mga lahat, sa kalahatan,

01:55:11.810 --> 01:55:13.370
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: meron

01:55:13.370 --> 01:55:15.930
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: po ba na nagdideklara o hindi nagdideklara?

01:55:16.290 --> 01:55:24.250
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Again, Your Honor, we do not check po yung mga items na nilalagay nila sa mga silence nila. We merely check as to the forms po.

01:55:26.580 --> 01:56:14.010
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With the indulgence of Senator Judge Sotto, if I may read into the records, Section 35 of the Omnibus Rules. Foreign currency. Personal properties such as cash on hand and in bank, as well as stocks and the like, denominated in foreign currency, shall be converted for purposes of declaration into the corresponding Philippine currency equivalent at the rate of exchange prevailing. A. On the date of assumption to office for those entering government service, B, as of December 31 of the preceding calendar year for the annual filing, and C, on the date of separation from the service for those leaving the government service. So dinedeklara po pero sa piso na po, hindi

01:56:14.010 --> 01:56:18.810
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: sa kung anumang foreign currency. All right. Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. My question was answered.

01:56:22.270 --> 01:56:22.870
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank

01:56:22.870 --> 01:56:23.390
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you, Your Honor.

01:56:25.150 --> 01:56:27.850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator-Judge Hontiveros is recognized.

01:56:37.310 --> 01:56:39.270
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

01:56:41.320 --> 01:57:04.890
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Madam Witness, isang clarificatory question lamang po para malinaw. Kapag stockholder ng kumpanya, tama po ba na considered personal property yung shares of stock at kailangan i-declare kung magkano yung acquisition cost? ng shares sa ilalim ng personal properties.

01:57:06.030 --> 01:57:15.170
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Your Honor, I'm sorry but I'm not in the position to answer that. As again, the Office of the Ombudsman is merely a repository agency of this Salen.

01:57:15.770 --> 01:57:36.780
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Alright. Kung ganun, salamat Madam Witness. Kung ganun po, Mr. Presiding Officer, kung pwede kong itanong yung prosecution at yung defense. So, Atty. James, kailangan bang i-deklara? kung magkano yung acquisition cost nung shares na yun sa ilalim ng personal properties kung shareholders sa kumpanya.

01:57:37.380 --> 01:57:52.420
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Salamat po sa tanong, Madam, Your Honor. Hindi na po ako sasagot po based on my knowledge but I'll just refer Your Honors to Section 8 of RA 6713.

01:57:52.700 --> 01:57:56.100
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes, yung Code of Conduct and Ethical Standards kung saan considered.

01:57:58.980 --> 01:58:02.360
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Asset ang stocks na dapat kasama sa SAL

01:58:02.360 --> 01:58:31.270
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: -N. So ayun po, without, so that I don't make any conclusions, Your Honor, I'll just refer the members of the Honorable Court to that Section 8 of Republic Act 6713 where it states na kailangan po parte ng SAL-N sa personal property at ang acquisition costs. At malinaw po doon ang ginagamit na word ay end. Acquisition cost in relation to personal property. Yan lang naman po ang sinasabi ng batas.

01:58:31.830 --> 01:58:45.830
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po Mr. Presiding Officer kasi yung unang nabasa ko pa lamang dun sa section 8 na yun ay all other assets such as investments, cash on hand or in banks, stocks, bonds, and the like.

01:58:45.950 --> 01:58:56.710
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Idagdag ko lang po your honors if you'll allow it with your kind permission po. Ang personal property po Kasama rin po yan. Based dun sa section na yan, kasama po dyan ang stocks and other

01:58:56.710 --> 01:59:12.290
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: investments. Okay. Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer. Kung may gustong i-comment din ang defense sa tanong ko tungkol dun sa kung kailangan ilista yung acquisition cost ng stocks sa ilalim ng personal properties kung shareholder sa kumpanya.

01:59:12.610 --> 01:59:24.590
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Thank you, Your Honor, for considering the side of the defense. But again, having in mind the position and reminders of the Presiding Officer, We defer matters of conclusions of law to each of you, Senator-Judges hereon.

01:59:24.690 --> 01:59:48.220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With the indulgence of Senator-Judge Riza, as earlier asked by the Presiding Officer, Atty. James, ba't wala sa form? Saan ko ilalagay kung gusto ko ilagay? You're correct in citing the law, but even if the official wanted to, where and how will he put it when we're supposed to fill out a prescribed form?

01:59:49.380 --> 01:59:50.200
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: May I respond?

01:59:50.280 --> 01:59:50.520
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Of

01:59:50.520 --> 01:59:50.740
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: course.

01:59:51.360 --> 02:00:00.960
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: I'm asking you, counsel. Your Honor, as I mentioned, this is not me mentioning this, it's just the law. Section 8, personal properties and... I

02:00:00.960 --> 02:00:36.170
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: agree with what the law says. Yesterday, your expert witness said it comes in a prescribed form. I asked if it was illegal for the President and Vice President to have business interests, then why do their forms still contain that? And she said it's a standard form. Fine. So it's a standard form. It's pro forma, she said. So why does this pro forma form? Not include a line or column for acquisition cost for businesses if that is the requirement of the law.

02:00:36.730 --> 02:00:37.870
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Your Honor, if I may?

02:00:38.090 --> 02:00:38.970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: If you know, counsel.

02:00:39.250 --> 02:00:40.750
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: I'll try my best to know, Your

02:00:40.750 --> 02:00:40.970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Honor.

02:00:42.230 --> 02:00:54.040
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Kasi po yung stocks is considered as personal property. So dapat po nandun sa personal property portion yung stocks. Hindi, nakahiwalay na table yun eh. As you said, you haven't filled out

02:00:54.040 --> 02:00:54.160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: the

02:00:54.160 --> 02:01:31.230
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: form. I'm not arguing, Your Honor. I understand the form that there are two portions, the business interest and the personal properties, Your Honor. And I'm not trying to influence the Honorable Court, but our understanding, Your Honor, is that because these are personal properties like investments, and if you look at the form, Your Honor, there is also no separate portion for investments because these are all considered as personal properties. And I think the CSC is in a better position to answer this. But based on our stand, Your Honor, it has to be included in the personal property if we are to believe that SAL-N should be... So

02:01:31.230 --> 02:01:32.150
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you lump it there?

02:01:33.210 --> 02:01:34.510
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Yes, Your Honor, that is our position.

02:01:34.870 --> 02:01:36.510
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You lump it there, personal properties?

02:01:36.850 --> 02:01:40.830
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Yes, and I may just add that it has to be itemized, Your Honor. That is our position.

02:01:41.810 --> 02:01:50.130
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: But that's not in the guidelines anymore as well, counsel. Anyway, Senator-Judge Riza, apologies for the interjection. Just to clarify.

02:01:50.830 --> 02:01:52.490
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:01:55.250 --> 02:02:47.050
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Ito pa po sa Section 30 on inclusion. Nasa omnibus rules po on SAL-N. Personal property refers to jewelry, appliances, furniture, motor vehicles, and other tangible movable properties of value. So, kitang-kita po natin sa forms kanina. This shall also include, nasabi ko na po, investments or other assets such as cash on hand or in the bank, negotiable instruments, securities, stocks, bonds, and the like. So, siguro yung huling observation ko na lamang po, Mr. Presiding Officer, hindi ko palang maalala sa puntong ito kung sino po sa impeachment trial na ito ay nagbanggit but I seem to recall na may nagbanggit na baka nga po kailangang Ammendahan baguhin i-improve yung form mismo para ma-deklara natin lahat na nagtatrabaho sa gobyerno

02:02:47.050 --> 02:02:48.450
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: yung hinihingi ng

02:02:48.450 --> 02:02:49.630
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: batas. That

02:02:49.630 --> 02:02:51.070
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: was discussed yesterday. Yes,

02:02:51.070 --> 02:03:01.070
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Mr. Presiding Officer. Salamat po sa parehong recollection din pala sa alaala ko. Salamat po, Madam Witness. Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:03:01.330 --> 02:03:03.490
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, the Senate President. Then we break for lunch.

02:03:10.070 --> 02:03:30.170
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Discussion on the corporations. Madam Witness, itong corporations, nakita ko sa mga SALN hindi naka-declare yung acquisition cost. So, ibig sabihin na may possibility na yung net worth is undervalued.

02:03:31.750 --> 02:03:33.930
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Kasi walang value yung mga corporations.

02:03:35.730 --> 02:03:57.170
Atty. Karen S. Batu: I cannot make that inference, Your Honor, kasi as I've said, the Office of the Ombudsman is merely a repository agency. So, as to the SALN po of anyone, kung undervalued yun dahil hindi po nag-declare ng acquisition costs, hindi po namin yun masasabi, Your Honor. Can

02:03:57.170 --> 02:04:14.440
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: I ask the prosecution, since you raised this non-declaration, is that the possibility na undervalued yung net worth? Because there's no value in the corporation. It's declared, but there's no value. Ibig sabihin the corporation, the acquisition cost might be millions.

02:04:16.020 --> 02:04:28.120
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Your Honor, without concluding anything, yes, it can be a possibility. That's why precisely, Your Honor, it has to be declared para po klaro at the onset kung ano po talaga yung...

02:04:30.760 --> 02:04:34.620
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: corresponding na amounts or value ng mga shares of stock. So

02:04:34.620 --> 02:04:42.100
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: yung napakita kanina ng mga pinakita mong mga net worth can be undervalued because walang value yung corporation eh.

02:04:42.260 --> 02:04:44.240
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Yes, Your Honor. That's a

02:04:44.240 --> 02:04:44.540
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: possibility. Alam naman

02:04:44.540 --> 02:04:45.260
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: yung liabilities.

02:04:45.540 --> 02:04:45.900
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: That's

02:04:45.900 --> 02:04:46.480
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: a possibility. Alam

02:04:46.480 --> 02:04:55.260
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: natin yung asset. But blanco yung acquisition cost for corporations. I would assume there's a value for that. Pag linagay mo yun, di lalaki yung net worth.

02:04:55.600 --> 02:04:58.420
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Opo. At yun po yung line of questioning ko kanina, Your Honor. That's the

02:04:58.420 --> 02:04:59.600
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: possibility po. Okay.

02:04:59.680 --> 02:05:18.450
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: And in that case, I was looking at the SAL-Ns. Tatanong ko ulit si Madam Witness. Kung that is the case, kailan pwedeng i-correct o lagyan ng value ng declarant yung mga corporations?

02:05:20.680 --> 02:05:34.650
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Kasi hindi natin, based dito sa SAL-N, hindi natin nakikita yung true net worth eh. Kasi walang value yung corporation. Ngayon, kung gusto na ngayon ng deklarant lagyan ng value, kailan niya pwedeng lagyan ng value?

02:05:35.710 --> 02:05:42.330
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Your Honor, again, the Office of the Ombudsman cannot make any comment on that. Kaya

02:05:42.330 --> 02:05:43.730
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: kung gusto lang niya i-correct, let's

02:05:43.730 --> 02:05:54.850
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: say gusto niya i-correct, or kagaya ng sinabi ni President Officer, nalito lang siya doon sa column, gusto niya nalagyan, kailan niya pwedeng, kailan ng deadline sa pagko-correct?

02:05:56.590 --> 02:06:29.720
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Ang submission po kasi natin ng SAL-N is every 30th of the April po, pero that's for the agency. So Office of the Ombudsman po, currently ang guidelines po namin states that ang submission po to the office as the repository agency is every 30th of June. So pag na-submit na po siya sa amin, Your Honor, as to the changes po pertaining to those assets, Aside from the form and other clerical or minimal error, hindi na po pwede, Your Honor.

02:06:29.940 --> 02:06:43.320
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So in other words, every year, kasi tinitignan ko yung pinasent na SAL-N, every year walang value yung corporation. So every year, possibility lang naman ito ah. There's a possibility na undervalued the net worth.

02:06:44.870 --> 02:06:45.350
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Kasi

02:06:45.350 --> 02:06:50.070
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: walang correction eh. Tinitignan ko itong pinasent na SAL-N.

02:06:50.440 --> 02:06:53.360
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Your Honor, I cannot make that inference based

02:06:53.360 --> 02:06:57.980
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: on the records. I'll ask the prosecution. Is that a possibility? I'm just saying whether it's

02:06:57.980 --> 02:06:58.960
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: a possibility or not.

02:06:59.460 --> 02:07:17.740
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Yes, Your Honor. I think that's also precisely why there is a corrective mechanism so that kung meron mang pumali na hindi sadya, pwede pong makorect. Ang problema lang po, pag tuloy-tuloy na wala namang tuloy-tuloy yung declaration, tapos wala namang pong correction. But I'll leave that judgment to the Honorable Court, Your Honor.

02:07:19.220 --> 02:07:34.200
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Balikan ko si Ms. Witness. Kanina nasabi ng ating former Senate President Tito Sotto yung foreign currency deposit. Kung meron kang foreign currency deposit, saan mo ilalagay siya? Saan mo i-declare siya in your SAL-N?

02:07:35.750 --> 02:07:40.050
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Your Honor, I haven't experienced declaring foreign currency deposit.

02:07:40.090 --> 02:07:47.390
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Since you're a custodian, you've been working in the Ombudsman for quite some time since 2010.

02:07:49.360 --> 02:07:54.740
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Kung may nagtanong sa iyo, saan ko i-declare yung dollar account ko? Saan niya ilalagay in the columns?

02:07:55.220 --> 02:08:00.300
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Generally, your owner bank deposits are declared under the personal properties.

02:08:00.620 --> 02:08:23.580
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: In personal properties. So doon niya ilalagay yung kanyang personal properties. Yung foreign currency deposits niya. Next will be, dito sa mga sal-ends ni VP Sara, may nakita ba kayong... Kulang sa declaration ng SAL-Ns? May years ba na kulang?

02:08:26.840 --> 02:08:29.940
Atty. Karen S. Batu: You mean po, Your Honor, meron pong year na hindi nag-submit?

02:08:30.000 --> 02:08:30.220
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Yes.

02:08:31.750 --> 02:08:39.010
Atty. Karen S. Batu: For 2013 po, Your Honor, wala po kaming record ng kanyang 2013 SAL-N.

02:08:39.870 --> 02:08:40.770
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: One year lang?

02:08:41.430 --> 02:08:45.910
Atty. Karen S. Batu: For 2014, wala din po.

02:08:46.010 --> 02:08:48.950
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So how many years ang kulang? Give me complete answers.

02:08:50.620 --> 02:09:01.240
Atty. Karen S. Batu: 2013 and 2014 po wala. May certification po yung Office of the Mindanao na wala pong silang nakitang on records ng 2013 and 2014 SAL-Ns.

02:09:01.500 --> 02:09:09.900
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: And then, nakita ko sa rules na pag bagong assumption mo sa office, kailangan mo rin mag-declare ng SAL-N, tama?

02:09:10.120 --> 02:09:10.780
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes, Your Honor.

02:09:11.340 --> 02:09:18.640
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Because of this rule, kompleto ba yung declaration ng VP Sara sa kanyang SAL-N?

02:09:20.170 --> 02:09:33.050
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Ang nakita lang po namin is for the 2013, wala po siyang exit SAL-N. As to the entry SAL-N, mukhang kompleto naman po. Yung exit SAL-N lang po ng 2013 na wala.

02:09:33.650 --> 02:09:47.210
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Yung itong dalawang years na sinabi niya walang SAL-N, ano ang corrective mechanism dyan? Assuming nakalimutan lang, assuming nakaligtaan ng accountant, kailan siya pwedeng mag-correct?

02:09:48.250 --> 02:09:48.790
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Based

02:09:48.790 --> 02:09:53.030
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: on your knowledge with itong ganitong declaration of SAL-N?

02:09:54.370 --> 02:10:15.250
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Based on my understanding po pagdating sa non-filing po ng SAL-N, kasi nga po may deadlines po as to the filing of SAL-N. Kung maglipapile po siya ng late, say after 30th of June, which is the deadline for the Office of the Ombudsman,

02:10:17.070 --> 02:10:20.590
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tatanggapin pa rin po namin yun but that would be labeled as a late filing.

02:10:21.510 --> 02:10:28.250
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Nasabi sa akin ng ating presiding officer in 2013-2014 di naman public official si VP

02:10:28.280 --> 02:10:32.380
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Sara. Parang nag-end po yung term niya noong 2013, June 30, 2013.

02:10:33.080 --> 02:10:34.980
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So ang dapat mag-file siya ng SAL-N?

02:10:35.180 --> 02:10:35.840
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes po.

02:10:35.980 --> 02:10:39.000
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Bago matapos yung kanyang...

02:10:39.000 --> 02:10:40.300
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Exit SAL-N po.

02:10:40.400 --> 02:10:54.020
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Yung exit SAL-N niya. And then, another question. Pag fina-file ba sa inyo, do you verify the correctness of the contents of the SAL-N? Ginagawa ba yan ng ombudsman?

02:10:54.260 --> 02:11:10.400
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Hindi po as to the correctness ng contents po, Your Honor. Chinicheck lang po namin kasi from time to time nagbabago po ng form ang Civil Service Commission. So, chinicheck lang po namin kung tama yung form na ginamit. Tapos kung minsan nakasign po.

02:11:18.620 --> 02:11:19.940
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Like for

02:11:19.940 --> 02:11:34.820
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: example, kanina na pinapakinggan ko yung mga corporations na undeclared. Nagkakaroon ba kayo, let's say, ng cross-reference with SEC para makita nyo kung declared siya o hindi? Meron bang ganyan na mga mechanisms to verify?

02:11:35.870 --> 02:11:44.770
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Your Honor, hindi po namin ginagawa yun because we only accept po yung mga sal-ends lang po ng mga public officials. No attachments needed po.

02:11:44.850 --> 02:11:46.350
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So ministerial lang tinatanggap

02:11:46.350 --> 02:11:46.850
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: niyo at

02:11:46.850 --> 02:11:48.530
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: repository lang kayo?

02:11:48.530 --> 02:11:49.690
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes po, Your Honor. Thank

02:11:49.690 --> 02:11:50.870
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:11:52.600 --> 02:11:58.020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Habol, bago mag-go, Senator-Judge Pangilinan, before we break for lunch, for your interjection.

02:11:58.160 --> 02:11:59.160
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Thank you,

02:11:59.280 --> 02:12:00.940
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:12:03.090 --> 02:12:04.190
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Atty. Batu,

02:12:06.210 --> 02:12:12.810
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Tinitingnan niyo, sabi niyo kanina, yung correctness nung filed SAL-N on the basis of yung form.

02:12:13.010 --> 02:12:14.050
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Opo, Your Honor.

02:12:14.290 --> 02:12:22.550
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Okay. Hindi ba yung SAL-N merong... Yung form niya, sabi niyo, nagbabago minsan based on CSE. Tama

02:12:22.550 --> 02:12:22.750
Atty. Karen S. Batu: po.

02:12:22.950 --> 02:12:30.970
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Okay. Pero alam ninyo na dito sa form na ito, merong one, two pages ata, merong...

02:12:32.480 --> 02:12:43.250
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Parang declaration on business interest on one hand. Pero meron din declaration on personal properties.

02:12:46.770 --> 02:12:47.950
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: So merong

02:12:47.950 --> 02:12:51.890
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: business interest, merong personal properties. Hindi ba sa form?

02:12:52.090 --> 02:12:53.050
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tama po. So

02:12:53.050 --> 02:13:21.850
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: tinitingnan niyo yun. So walang acquisition cost area sa business interest. Pero naalala ko kasi kahapon sabi ni Justice Cabotaje Tang na based on the law, kinakailangan yung personal properties dinedeklara. So there is a separate declaration or form sa form yung personal property declaration, di ba?

02:13:22.010 --> 02:13:22.430
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Opo.

02:13:22.530 --> 02:13:41.080
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: At naroon sa personal property declaration yung acquisition cost. Nandun po. Okay, so it may not be indeed... Business interest form, part of the form, but it is in the personal properties part of the form yung nire-require yung acquisition cost.

02:13:41.380 --> 02:13:42.380
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Tama po, Your Honor.

02:13:42.600 --> 02:13:52.940
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Okay, yun lang. Just to clarify that. So may requirement ng acquisition cost for personal properties and shares would be considered personal property?

02:13:54.840 --> 02:13:57.880
Atty. Karen S. Batu: Yes po, meron po tayong acquisition cost.

02:14:18.720 --> 02:14:22.760
Sen. Francis Pangilinan: Thank you. You just clarified that.

02:14:24.510 --> 02:14:39.620
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: That's what I do too in my cell and for my law firm, Senator-Judge Pangilinan. I put it there in personal property para may acquisition. Anyway, let's break for lunch. We shall resume at 12.45.

